// RFC-018 stage-two footprints for the rpi-pico2 board: real pad geometry
// for every footprint the board's own parts bind. Pad symbols resolve to the
// std pad library (std/pads.cohdl) through the std prelude; pad NUMBERS match
// each bound device's declared pin numbers (RFC-002), so `cohdl build`'s
// E807 pad-consistency check passes. Each `was:` comment records the KiCad
// footprint id the geometry derives from (or the datasheet/IPC-7351 nominal
// land pattern where KiCad ships no exact match — the Wuerth micro-USB
// hand-solder land, the USON-8 1.0x1.5 / WQFN-10 packages, the 0806 inductor,
// and the Pico castellated headers). Geometry feeds the .kicad_mod / IPC-2581
// projection (RFC-015/018); it is nominal land-pattern data for partner
// layout (Quilter), not a placement.

// was: "Package_DFN_QFN:QFN-60-1EP_7x7mm_P0.4mm_EP3.5x3.5mm"
// IPC-7351 name (RFC-021): 60 leads, density N, 0.40mm pitch, 7.00x7.00mm
